1:1-1 (* EXPECT-ERROR: the answer of View dies with this frame *)
2:1-13 (* This is the builder's view that outlived its frame.  DynUtf.View\n   answers a validated COPY of the builder's octets, `RETURN UTF (...)`,\n   where DynStr.View answered a view into the builder's pool.  On\n   2026-10-23 three ports of the compiler to UTF kept such an answer in\n   module state: Sem's message list (a diagnostic read as blank), Gen's\n   typedef dedup key (one typedef emitted twice), and m9c's own output\n   file names (`cannot read or write: <NULs and generated C>`, every\n   genforms build red).  `--check` accepted all three.  The checker knew\n   `+` and a frame NEW as what a callee's RETURN could build in the\n   caller's frame, and not the UTF builtins.  This is the shape, without\n   the library: a function that answers `UTF (text)`, stored where the\n   frame it was built in will not be. *)
comments=2
